    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11-a1">

                <pb facs="0102" n="18" xml:id="pg18"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Strauss to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1903</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I have received your favor informing
                    me that you would communicate with the American representative at Vienna in
                    regard to the form of certificate required to show that Austrian subjects are
                    admitted to trade in the United States.</p>
                <p>I am informed by my correspondent at Vienna that a mere statement to the effect
                    that Austrian subjects are admitted to trade in the United States will be
                    sufficient, the purpose being merely to assure and preserve relations of
                    reciprocity between the citizens of the two countries. I desire to make clear
                    that the only purpose of the certificate is in connection with the application
                    of John Underwood &amp; Co., dealers in typewriter supplies, to be permitted to
                    open a branch of their business at Vienna.</p>
                <p>If, in view of this statement of facts, the delay of awaiting communication from
                    abroad can be avoided we should be very glad, as otherwise we are subjected to
                    much inconvenience and possible loss.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. Strauss.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
